                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This is a compulsory course for five‑year undergraduate students majoring in Stomatology, worth 1 credit with 16 class hours of theoretical lectures. It mainly introduces fundamental knowledge, clinical applications, cutting‑edge advances and medicine‑engineering interdisciplinary research of biomedical materials related to stomatology. The course consists of two major parts: basic knowledge of dental materials and clinical dental materials. The basic‑knowledge section covers the introduction to dental materials, fundamentals and properties of materials, as well as clinical applications of common dental materials.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
